  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Centre on Biodiversity for Climate (GCBC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Centre on Biodiversity for Climate (GCBC) is an Official Development Assistance (ODA) research programme funded by the UK Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (Defra). Its aim is to generate evidence on how the protection, restoration and sustainable use of biodiversity can strengthen climate resilience and reduce poverty. Through a global network of researchers, practitioners and communities, GCBC seeks to advance understanding of the interconnected challenges of biodiversity loss, climate change and poverty, while ensuring that research findings inform policy and practice at national and international scales. For more information, please visit www.gcbc.org.uk</narrative>
  </description>
